WEBVTT

00:00.630 --> 00:02.810
We now know that if
we have two triangles

00:02.810 --> 00:05.110
and all of their
corresponding sides

00:05.110 --> 00:07.910
are the same, so by
side, side, side-- so

00:07.910 --> 00:09.670
if the corresponding
sides, all three

00:09.670 --> 00:12.150
of the corresponding sides,
have the same length,

00:12.150 --> 00:15.034
we know that those
triangles are congruent.

00:15.034 --> 00:16.450
What I want to do
in this video is

00:16.450 --> 00:18.540
explore if there
are other properties

00:18.540 --> 00:20.750
that we can find between
the triangles that

00:20.750 --> 00:23.870
can help us feel pretty good
that those two triangles would

00:23.870 --> 00:25.110
be congruent.

00:25.110 --> 00:26.690
So side, side, side works.

00:26.690 --> 00:28.770
What about angle, angle, angle?

00:28.770 --> 00:30.210
So let me do that over here.

00:30.210 --> 00:31.860
What about angle angle angle?

00:31.860 --> 00:33.840
So what I'm saying
is, is if-- let's say

00:33.840 --> 00:36.060
I have a triangle
like this, like I

00:36.060 --> 00:39.640
have a triangle like that, and
I have a triangle like this.

00:39.640 --> 00:44.550
And if we know that this angle
is congruent to that angle,

00:44.550 --> 00:47.660
if this angle is congruent
to that angle, which

00:47.660 --> 00:51.610
means that their measures are
equal, or-- and-- I should say

00:51.610 --> 00:55.100
and-- and that angle is
congruent to that angle,

00:55.100 --> 00:59.350
can we say that these are
two congruent triangles?

00:59.350 --> 01:01.870
And at first case, it
looks like maybe it

01:01.870 --> 01:03.470
is, at least the
way I drew it here.

01:03.470 --> 01:04.970
But when you think
about it, you can

01:04.970 --> 01:08.616
have the exact same
corresponding angles,

01:08.616 --> 01:10.830
having the same measure
or being congruent,

01:10.830 --> 01:13.760
but you could actually scale one
of these triangles up and down

01:13.760 --> 01:15.390
and still have that property.

01:15.390 --> 01:20.840
For example, if I had this
triangle right over here,

01:20.840 --> 01:23.630
it looks similar--
and I'm using that

01:23.630 --> 01:25.550
in just the everyday
language sense--

01:25.550 --> 01:28.740
it has the same shape as these
triangles right over here.

01:28.740 --> 01:31.650
And it has the same angles.

01:31.650 --> 01:34.070
That angle is congruent
to that angle,

01:34.070 --> 01:36.700
this angle down here is
congruent to this angle

01:36.700 --> 01:39.570
over here, and this
angle over here

01:39.570 --> 01:41.510
is congruent to this
angle over here.

01:41.510 --> 01:44.020
So all of the angles in all
three of these triangles

01:44.020 --> 01:44.800
are the same.

01:44.800 --> 01:47.080
The corresponding angles
have the same measure.

01:47.080 --> 01:50.690
But clearly, clearly this
triangle right over here

01:50.690 --> 01:52.010
is not the same.

01:52.010 --> 01:54.120
It is not congruent
to the other two.

01:54.120 --> 01:56.940
The sides have a very
different length.

01:56.940 --> 01:59.850
This side is much shorter than
this side right over here.

01:59.850 --> 02:02.500
This side is much shorter
than that side over there.

02:02.500 --> 02:04.650
And this side is much
shorter over here.

02:04.650 --> 02:06.580
So with just angle,
angle, angle,

02:06.580 --> 02:11.090
you cannot say that a triangle
has the same size and shape.

02:11.090 --> 02:14.070
It does have the same shape
but not the same size.

02:14.070 --> 02:18.530
So this does not
imply congruency.

02:18.530 --> 02:21.400
So angle, angle, angle
does not imply congruency.

02:21.400 --> 02:24.130
What it does imply, and we
haven't talked about this yet,

02:24.130 --> 02:26.500
is that these are
similar triangles.

02:26.500 --> 02:29.012
So angle, angle,
angle implies similar.

02:29.012 --> 02:30.220
So let me write it over here.

02:30.220 --> 02:32.250
It implies similar triangles.

02:32.250 --> 02:33.975
And similar-- you
probably are use

02:33.975 --> 02:36.100
to the word in just everyday
language-- but similar

02:36.100 --> 02:39.190
has a very specific
meaning in geometry.

02:39.190 --> 02:42.500
And similar things have
the same shape but not

02:42.500 --> 02:44.800
necessarily the same size.

02:44.800 --> 02:47.050
So anything that is
congruent, because it

02:47.050 --> 02:50.120
has the same size and
shape, is also similar.

02:50.120 --> 02:53.030
But not everything that is
similar is also congruent.

02:53.030 --> 02:56.910
So for example, this
triangle is similar-- all

02:56.910 --> 02:59.080
of these triangles are
similar to each other,

02:59.080 --> 03:00.520
but they aren't all congruent.

03:00.520 --> 03:02.215
These two are congruent
if their sides

03:02.215 --> 03:04.090
are the same-- I didn't
make that assumption.

03:04.090 --> 03:06.096
But if we know that
their sides are the same,

03:06.096 --> 03:07.720
then we can say that
they're congruent.

03:07.720 --> 03:10.050
But neither of these are
congruent to this one right

03:10.050 --> 03:12.030
over here, because this
is clearly much larger.

03:12.030 --> 03:14.530
It has the same shape
but a different size.

03:14.530 --> 03:18.590
So we can't have an AAA
postulate or an AAA axiom

03:18.590 --> 03:20.820
to get to congruency.

03:20.820 --> 03:23.220
What about side, angle, side?

03:23.220 --> 03:26.880
So let's try this out,
side, angle, side.

03:26.880 --> 03:29.727
So let's start off with one
triangle right over here.

03:29.727 --> 03:32.060
So let's start off with a
triangle that looks like this.

03:32.060 --> 03:35.010
I have my blue side,
I have my pink side,

03:35.010 --> 03:37.410
and I have my magenta side.

03:37.410 --> 03:40.410
And let's say that I have
another triangle that

03:40.410 --> 03:42.520
has this blue side.

03:42.520 --> 03:45.670
It has the same side, same
length as that blue side.

03:45.670 --> 03:47.530
So let me draw it like that.

03:47.530 --> 03:49.820
It has the same length
as that blue side.

03:49.820 --> 03:53.180
So that length and that length
are going to be the same.

03:53.180 --> 03:56.170
It has a congruent
angle right after that.

03:56.170 --> 04:00.020
So this angle and the next
angle for this triangle

04:00.020 --> 04:02.496
are going to have
the same measure,

04:02.496 --> 04:03.870
or they're going
to be congruent.

04:03.870 --> 04:07.207
And then the next
side is going to have

04:07.207 --> 04:08.790
the same length as
this one over here.

04:08.790 --> 04:12.360
So that's going to be the
same length as this over here.

04:12.360 --> 04:15.140
So it's going to
be the same length.

04:15.140 --> 04:20.490
And because we only know that
two of the corresponding sides

04:20.490 --> 04:23.119
have the same length, and
the angle between them--

04:23.119 --> 04:25.160
and this is important--
the angle between the two

04:25.160 --> 04:28.630
corresponding sides also
have the same measure,

04:28.630 --> 04:32.230
we can do anything we want with
this last side on this one.

04:32.230 --> 04:33.855
We can essentially--
it's going to have

04:33.855 --> 04:35.540
to start right over here.

04:35.540 --> 04:36.980
You could start from this point.

04:36.980 --> 04:39.940
And we can pivot it to
form any triangle we want.

04:39.940 --> 04:42.065
But we can see, the only
way we can form a triangle

04:42.065 --> 04:44.170
is if we bring this side
all the way over here

04:44.170 --> 04:46.560
and close this right over there.

04:46.560 --> 04:51.780
And so we can see just
logically for two triangles,

04:51.780 --> 04:54.540
they have one side that
has the length the same,

04:54.540 --> 04:56.260
the next side has
a length the same,

04:56.260 --> 04:59.710
and the angle in between
them-- so this angle--

04:59.710 --> 05:02.080
let me do that in the
same color-- this angle in

05:02.080 --> 05:03.570
between them, this is the angle.

05:03.570 --> 05:06.310
This A is this angle
and that angle.

05:06.310 --> 05:08.080
It's the angle in between them.

05:08.080 --> 05:10.590
This first side is in blue.

05:10.590 --> 05:13.716
And this second side right,
over here, is in pink.

05:13.716 --> 05:15.490
Well, it's already
written in pink.

05:15.490 --> 05:17.770
So we can see that if two
sides are the same, have

05:17.770 --> 05:19.760
the same length-- two
corresponding sides have

05:19.760 --> 05:21.593
the same length, and
the corresponding angle

05:21.593 --> 05:23.950
between them, they
have to be congruent.

05:23.950 --> 05:27.000
There's no other one place
to put this third side.

05:27.000 --> 05:29.270
So SAS-- and sometimes,
it's once again

05:29.270 --> 05:32.230
called a postulate, an axiom,
or if it's kind of proven,

05:32.230 --> 05:34.500
sometimes is called
a theorem-- this

05:34.500 --> 05:38.594
does imply that the two
triangles are congruent.

05:38.594 --> 05:40.760
So we will give ourselves
this tool in our tool kit.

05:40.760 --> 05:42.960
We had the SSS postulate.

05:42.960 --> 05:45.320
Now we have the SAS postulate.

05:45.320 --> 05:47.830
Two sides are equal and
the angle in between them,

05:47.830 --> 05:50.730
for two triangles,
corresponding sides and angles,

05:50.730 --> 05:53.120
then we can say that
it is definitely--

05:53.120 --> 05:55.362
these are congruent triangles.

05:55.362 --> 05:56.820
Now what about--
and I'm just going

05:56.820 --> 06:00.900
to try to go through all the
different combinations here--

06:00.900 --> 06:04.170
what if I have
angle, side, angle?

06:04.170 --> 06:05.730
So let me try that.

06:05.730 --> 06:09.420
So what happens if I
have angle, side, angle?

06:09.420 --> 06:12.232
So let's go back to this
one right over here.

06:12.232 --> 06:13.940
So actually, let me
just redraw a new one

06:13.940 --> 06:15.640
for each of these cases.

06:15.640 --> 06:20.230
So angle, side, angle, so
I'll draw a triangle here.

06:20.230 --> 06:22.160
So I have this triangle.

06:22.160 --> 06:24.500
So this would be maybe the side.

06:24.500 --> 06:25.816
That would be the side.

06:25.816 --> 06:27.940
So let me draw the whole
triangle, actually, first.

06:27.940 --> 06:29.460
So I have this triangle.

06:29.460 --> 06:31.600
Let me draw one side over here.

06:31.600 --> 06:34.090
And then let me draw
one side over there.

06:34.090 --> 06:36.650
And this angle right
over here, I'll

06:36.650 --> 06:39.230
call it-- I'll do it in orange.

06:39.230 --> 06:43.790
And this angle over here,
I will do it in yellow.

06:43.790 --> 06:45.560
So if I have another
triangle that

06:45.560 --> 06:49.449
has one side having
equal measure--

06:49.449 --> 06:51.490
so I'll use it as this
blue side right over here.

06:51.490 --> 06:53.940
So it has one side
that has equal measure.

06:53.940 --> 06:56.730
And the two angles on
either side of that side,

06:56.730 --> 06:59.610
or at either end of
that side, are the same,

06:59.610 --> 07:01.505
will this triangle
necessarily be congruent?

07:01.505 --> 07:03.380
And we're just going to
try to reason it out.

07:03.380 --> 07:04.570
These aren't formal proofs.

07:04.570 --> 07:05.986
We're really just
trying to set up

07:05.986 --> 07:07.680
what are reasonable
postulates, or what

07:07.680 --> 07:11.400
are reasonable assumptions
we can have in our tool kit

07:11.400 --> 07:13.370
as we try to prove other things.

07:13.370 --> 07:17.625
So that angle, let's call it
that angle, right over there,

07:17.625 --> 07:20.130
they're going to have the
same measure in this triangle.

07:20.130 --> 07:22.497
And this angle right
over here in yellow

07:22.497 --> 07:24.580
is going to have the same
measure on this triangle

07:24.580 --> 07:26.030
right over here.

07:26.030 --> 07:28.570
So regardless,
I'm not in any way

07:28.570 --> 07:30.130
constraining the
sides over here.

07:30.130 --> 07:33.700
So this side right over
here could have any length.

07:33.700 --> 07:37.340
It could have any length, but it
has to form this angle with it.

07:37.340 --> 07:38.506
So it could have any length.

07:38.506 --> 07:40.830
And it can just go as
far as it wants to go.

07:40.830 --> 07:43.490
In no way have we constrained
what the length of that is.

07:43.490 --> 07:45.290
And actually, let me
mark this off, too.

07:45.290 --> 07:47.230
So this is the same as this.

07:47.230 --> 07:48.570
So that side can be anything.

07:48.570 --> 07:50.040
We haven't constrained it all.

07:50.040 --> 07:53.160
And once again, this
side could be anything.

07:53.160 --> 07:54.690
We haven't
constrained it at all.

07:54.690 --> 07:56.630
But we know it has
to go at this angle.

07:56.630 --> 07:58.410
So it has to go at that angle.

07:58.410 --> 08:00.424
Well, once again,
there's only one triangle

08:00.424 --> 08:01.590
that can be formed this way.

08:01.590 --> 08:03.298
We can say all day
that this length could

08:03.298 --> 08:05.230
be as long as we want
or as short as we want.

08:05.230 --> 08:06.900
And this one could be as
long as we want and as short

08:06.900 --> 08:07.750
as we want.

08:07.750 --> 08:10.083
But the only way that they
can actually touch each other

08:10.083 --> 08:12.760
and form a triangle and
have these two angles,

08:12.760 --> 08:18.390
is if they are the exact same
length as these two sides

08:18.390 --> 08:19.140
right over here.

08:19.140 --> 08:22.761
So this side will actually have
to be the same as that side.

08:22.761 --> 08:24.760
And this would have to
be the same as that side.

08:24.760 --> 08:26.790
Once again, this isn't a proof.

08:26.790 --> 08:30.080
I'd call it more of a reasoning
through it or an investigation,

08:30.080 --> 08:32.919
really just to establish
what reasonable baselines,

08:32.919 --> 08:36.120
or axioms, or assumptions, or
postulates that we could have.

08:36.120 --> 08:40.070
So for my purposes, I
think ASA does show us

08:40.070 --> 08:44.727
that two triangles
are congruent.

08:44.727 --> 08:45.810
Now let's try another one.

08:45.810 --> 08:49.010
Let's try angle, angle, side.

08:49.010 --> 08:50.510
Let's try angle, angle, side.

08:50.510 --> 08:52.571
And in some geometry
classes, maybe

08:52.571 --> 08:54.320
if you have to go
through an exam quickly,

08:54.320 --> 08:57.086
you might memorize, OK, side,
side, side implies congruency.

08:57.086 --> 08:58.210
And that's kind of logical.

08:58.210 --> 08:59.751
Side, angle, side
implies congruency,

08:59.751 --> 09:01.660
and so on, and so forth.

09:01.660 --> 09:03.140
I'm not a fan of memorizing it.

09:03.140 --> 09:04.880
It might be good
for time pressure.

09:04.880 --> 09:07.470
It is good to, sometimes, even
just go through this logic.

09:07.470 --> 09:09.420
If you're like, wait, does
angle, angle, angle work?

09:09.420 --> 09:10.878
Well, no, I can
find this case that

09:10.878 --> 09:12.440
breaks down angle, angle, angle.

09:12.440 --> 09:14.540
If these work, just try
to verify for yourself

09:14.540 --> 09:17.880
that they make logical sense
why they would imply congruency.

09:17.880 --> 09:20.910
Now, let's try
angle, angle, side.

09:20.910 --> 09:24.620
Let's try angle, angle, side.

09:24.620 --> 09:27.670
So once again, let's have
a triangle over here.

09:27.670 --> 09:28.936
It has some side.

09:28.936 --> 09:31.310
So this one is going to be a
little bit more interesting.

09:31.310 --> 09:32.270
So it has some side.

09:32.270 --> 09:34.184
That's the side
right over there.

09:34.184 --> 09:35.350
And then, it has two angles.

09:35.350 --> 09:38.750
So let me draw the other
sides of this triangle.

09:38.750 --> 09:42.000
I'll draw one in magenta
and then one in green.

09:42.000 --> 09:45.720
And there's two angles
and then the side.

09:45.720 --> 09:48.200
So let's say you
have this angle-- you

09:48.200 --> 09:49.650
have that angle
right over there.

09:49.650 --> 09:50.720
Actually, I didn't
have to put a double,

09:50.720 --> 09:53.053
because that's the first angle
that I'm-- So I have that

09:53.053 --> 09:55.580
angle, which we'll refer
to as that first A.

09:55.580 --> 10:01.110
Then we have this angle,
which is that second A.

10:01.110 --> 10:05.570
So if I know that there's
another triangle that

10:05.570 --> 10:08.860
has one side having the
same length-- so let me draw

10:08.860 --> 10:11.680
it like that-- it has one
side having the same length.

10:11.680 --> 10:16.140
It has one angle on that side
that has the same measure.

10:16.140 --> 10:18.520
So it has a measure like that.

10:18.520 --> 10:23.950
And so this side right over
here could be of any length.

10:23.950 --> 10:26.590
We aren't constraining what
the length of that side is.

10:26.590 --> 10:28.980
But whatever the angle is on
the other side of that side

10:28.980 --> 10:32.350
is going to be the same as this
green angle right over here.

10:32.350 --> 10:34.327
So for example, it
could be like that.

10:34.327 --> 10:36.410
And then you could have a
green side go like that.

10:36.410 --> 10:39.650
It could be like that and have
the green side go like that.

10:39.650 --> 10:41.560
And if we have--
so the only thing

10:41.560 --> 10:46.490
we're assuming is that this
is the same length as this,

10:46.490 --> 10:49.360
and that this angle is the
same measure as that angle,

10:49.360 --> 10:51.710
and that this measure is the
same measure as that angle.

10:51.710 --> 10:54.390
And this magenta line
can be of any length,

10:54.390 --> 10:56.330
and this green line
can be of any length.

10:56.330 --> 10:58.440
We in no way have
constrained that.

10:58.440 --> 11:01.590
But can we form any triangle
that is not congruent to this?

11:01.590 --> 11:04.000
Because the bottom line
is, this green line

11:04.000 --> 11:06.330
is going to touch this
one right over there.

11:06.330 --> 11:10.040
And the only way it's going to
touch that one right over there

11:10.040 --> 11:13.370
is if it starts right
over here, because we're

11:13.370 --> 11:15.210
constraining this
angle right over here.

11:15.210 --> 11:16.970
We're constraining that angle.

11:16.970 --> 11:18.630
And so it looks
like angle, angle,

11:18.630 --> 11:23.220
side does indeed
imply congruency.

11:23.220 --> 11:26.110
So that does imply congruency.

11:26.110 --> 11:28.860
So let's just do one more
just to kind of try out

11:28.860 --> 11:30.806
all of the different situations.

11:30.806 --> 11:32.180
What if we have--
and I'm running

11:32.180 --> 11:33.240
out of a little
bit of real estate

11:33.240 --> 11:34.970
right over here at
the bottom-- what

11:34.970 --> 11:39.030
if we tried out
side, side, angle?

11:39.030 --> 11:42.000
So once again, draw a triangle.

11:42.000 --> 11:44.310
So it has one side there.

11:44.310 --> 11:46.710
It has another side there.

11:46.710 --> 11:49.750
And then-- I don't have to
do those hash marks just yet.

11:49.750 --> 11:54.497
So one side, then another
side, and then another side.

11:54.497 --> 11:57.080
And what happens if we know that
there's another triangle that

11:57.080 --> 12:00.470
has two of the sides the same
and then the angle after it?

12:00.470 --> 12:04.480
So for example, we would have
that side just like that,

12:04.480 --> 12:05.940
and then it has another side.

12:05.940 --> 12:09.540
But we're not
constraining the angle.

12:09.540 --> 12:11.910
We aren't constraining
this angle right over here,

12:11.910 --> 12:14.021
but we're constraining
the length of that side.

12:14.021 --> 12:15.020
So let me color code it.

12:15.020 --> 12:17.500
So that blue side
is that first side.

12:17.500 --> 12:21.150
Then we have this magenta
side right over there.

12:21.150 --> 12:23.835
So this is going to be the same
length as this right over here.

12:23.835 --> 12:25.460
But let me make it
at a different angle

12:25.460 --> 12:27.350
to see if I can disprove it.

12:27.350 --> 12:29.270
So let's say it looks like that.

12:29.270 --> 12:31.840
Or actually let me make
it even more interesting.

12:36.340 --> 12:39.600
Let me try to make it like that.

12:39.600 --> 12:41.090
So it's a very different angle.

12:41.090 --> 12:43.600
But now, it has to have
the same angle out here.

12:43.600 --> 12:45.700
It has to have that
same angle out here.

12:45.700 --> 12:47.640
So it has to be
roughly that angle.

12:47.640 --> 12:50.680
So it actually looks like we
can draw a triangle that is not

12:50.680 --> 12:54.429
congruent that has two
sides being the same length

12:54.429 --> 12:55.720
and then an angle is different.

12:55.720 --> 12:57.660
For example, this
is pretty much that.

12:57.660 --> 13:00.550
I made this angle
smaller than this angle.

13:00.550 --> 13:02.250
These two sides are the same.

13:02.250 --> 13:05.495
This angle is the same now, but
what the byproduct of that is,

